# apps/server/.dockerignore — informational pointer (DO NOT edit expecting effect)
#
# IMPORTANT: Docker only honors a single .dockerignore located at the BUILD CONTEXT
# ROOT, not next to the Dockerfile. The server image is built with:
#
#     docker build -f apps/server/Dockerfile -t xyz-agent-server:dev .        # from repo root
#     docker compose -f apps/server/compose.yml build                          # context: ../.. (repo root)
#
# Both invoke the repo root as context, so the EFFECTIVE .dockerignore is:
#
#     <repo-root>/.dockerignore
#
# This file exists only to make that explicit to anyone looking next to the
# Dockerfile (a common reflex). The real exclusion rules (node_modules, .git,
# apps/electron/resources pi binary, dist, docs, tools, .xyz-harness, test
# artifacts, etc.) live in the root .dockerignore. Keep that file in sync if
# you add new large or sensitive paths.
#
# Why a pointer instead of a duplicate: a copy here would be silently ignored
# by Docker and inevitably drift out of sync with the root file, giving a false
# sense of context filtering.
